fahrplan2 (2.0.51-meego1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: the DB (Deutsche Bahn) backend could not search at all on the device
    -- every request came back as VALIDIERUNG. The Qt 4 JSON serializer did
    not handle QStringList values (locationTypes, verkehrsmittel, ...); it
    dropped them and produced invalid JSON. QStringList is now serialized,
    and the container loops are counting loops (a Q_FOREACH body runs only
    once under a newer GCC). Affects every backend that posts JSON (DB, Matka).

 -- smatkovi <smatkovi@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:33:17 +0200

fahrplan2 (2.0.50-meego1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New backend: Netherlands (9292). A fresh client against the app host
    wrapper.9292.nl -- not the old parser, which spoke to the now-closed
    web-api.9292.nl. Station search and journey planning; the required
    per-request x-api-token (HMAC-SHA256) is computed with a self-contained
    SHA-256, so no extra library is pulled in.

 -- smatkovi <smatkovi@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:33:24 +0200

fahrplan2 (2.0.49-meego1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Transitous: a new station search no longer waits for the previous one.
    While a request was still in flight every further search was dropped, so
    typing a name could look as if the backend did nothing at all. The old
    request is cancelled instead, and an abort of our own stays quiet.

 -- smatkovi <smatkovi@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:15:00 +0200

fahrplan2 (2.0.48-meego1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New backend: Worldwide (Transitous), backported from upstream 2.0.58 to
    Qt 4.7 -- MOTIS API over https://api.transitous.org
  * Fix backend selection: with ninetwo removed, every backend after Ireland
    was off by one and picking one of them started bahn.de instead
  * About page: data source credits for transitous.org and OpenStreetMap
  * bahn.de: follow upstream to the moved endpoint (app.services-bahn.de)
    and to v9 of the journey search, which is why the old one answered
    nothing that could be parsed

 -- smatkovi <smatkovi@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:45:00 +0200

